 "relevance_note": "Single-patient case report of adult-onset Alexander disease with a GFAP variant: \"NGS found a heterozygous variant of unknown significance in GFAP (c.173T>C; p.L58P)\".",
 "method_note": "Written by hand with a short Python script that only assembles the JSON; no table transcription (the paper has no tables). One in-scope person, labelled 'patient' (rule 5). The pedigree (Figure 1) is not available as text, so no relatives get rows; family history of neurologic disorders was stated negative but that is not a feature of the patient, so it is not recorded. Age at onset left not reported: the paper gives onset only relative to a head injury, and two statements differ on timing ('first reported symptoms after a mild traumatic brain injury approximately 1 year before' vs. MRI 'immediately after the brain injury and 1 year before symptom onset'); no age at onset is computed. Age 57 recorded as age at report. Inheritance and parental testing not reported in text (pedigree marks alleles only in the figure). Pathogenicity: authors first categorized the variant as VUS, then call it a novel causal mutation after in vitro work; both recorded. Checklist: 'cerebral white matter abnormality' and 'periventricular rim' left not reported because the periventricular hyperintensities are described as surrounding the fourth ventricle and the Figure 2 legend does not say which ventricle; 'autonomic dysfunction' marked excluded from the explicit statement that autonomic dysfunction was not present, although sleep apnea is not addressed. 'limb weakness' marked observed from 'generalized muscle weakness'. Volumetry finding of striatal volume abnormality also supports basal ganglia involvement. The mild traumatic brain injury is recorded only in this note, not as a feature.",
