    "functional_evidence_statement": {
     "value": "In HeLa cells, wild-type GFAP assembled into bundled filaments whereas GFAP-L58P formed clusters of cytoplasmic aggregates, which were positive for αB-crystallin",
     "span": [
      "Fluorescence images showed that wild-type GFAP assembled into bundled filaments that extended throughout the cytoplasm, whereas GFAP-L58P formed clusters of cytoplasmic aggregates (Figure 3B)",
      "The GFAP containing aggregates in the cells transfected with GFAP-L58P gene were positive for αB-crystallin."
     ]
    },
